WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:05.330
Previously on Smallville, I picked out a nice little font for my expose.

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:08.330
I actually had another headline in mind.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:11.330
The blur murders Lois Lane.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:19.600
Out there somewhere.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.600
I've been keeping an eye on you.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:22.600
I have to see you.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.600
How do you feel about phone booth?

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.600
Hello?

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.600
This is the red-blue blur.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.600
I received your letter.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:31.600
What I've really been wondering is, what is it that you need?

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.600
I need your help, but you can't tell anyone about it.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.600
I promise.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.600
I wouldn't ask Lois if it weren't a matter.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.600
Ask Lois if it weren't a matter of life or death.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.600
Welcome to checkmate.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.600
You've been blocked by a new player.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:54.929
How do you get yourself into these things, Lane?

00:00:54.929 --> 00:01:01.539
Good to see.

00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:03.539
An honor, sir. Hey.

00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:06.540
Guys inside, bosses, we want to show it to you.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.540
He wants to collect a million dollar reward.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.540
Really?

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.540
Hi, Ray.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:11.540
Ladies.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.540
Hey, no, thanks.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.540
Hey, Bob.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:15.540
My old friend.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.540
It's been too long.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:17.540
Hey, how you doing?

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.540
Hey.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:24.549
Glad to have you back, Ray.

00:01:24.549 --> 00:01:26.549
Oh, good to be back, darling.

00:01:26.549 --> 00:01:28.549
Your coat, sir?

00:01:28.549 --> 00:01:30.900
Thanks, sweetie.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:52.670
Go right in.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:55.670
As your ex-District attorney,

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:58.670
I'd like to thank you all for joining me

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:01.670
in celebrating the national treasure

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:05.670
that is our American justice system.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:09.669
You know, they kicked me out of office.

00:02:09.669 --> 00:02:10.669
They charged me out of office.

00:02:10.669 --> 00:02:11.669
They charged me.

00:02:11.669 --> 00:02:13.169
with attempted murder.

00:02:13.169 --> 00:02:16.669
They even tried to put me away for life, and yet,

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:34.930
here I am.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:38.930
So, I understand you have something from me.

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:41.930
What about my million dollars?

00:02:41.930 --> 00:03:37.620
Don't test me, son.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:38.620
Find the story.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:40.620
Not be the story?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:53.180
You want to tell me what happened?

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:54.180
Let me guess.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:57.180
You two have a lover's spat.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:01.009
Clark and I don't spat.

00:04:01.009 --> 00:04:03.009
There was no spatting.

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:08.009
What Lois is saying is that we try not to let our personal lives get in the way of our jobs.

00:04:08.009 --> 00:05:41.139
Well, you don't have to try anymore, because you're both fired.

00:05:41.139 --> 00:05:45.139
Early is when you arrive at your destination by said time, not when you can see it from seven blocks away.

00:05:45.139 --> 00:05:49.139
Uh-uh. Nobody's raining on this girl's parade today.

00:05:49.139 --> 00:05:53.139
Clark's taking me up to the roof tonight to do a little stargazing.

00:05:53.139 --> 00:05:57.139
Okay, that explains the 911 to the Craigslist Queen.

00:05:57.139 --> 00:05:59.139
Long love the Queen.

00:05:59.139 --> 00:06:01.139
I can't believe you got one so fast.

00:06:01.139 --> 00:06:05.139
I kind of noticed that Clark has this thing for telescopes.

00:06:05.139 --> 00:06:07.139
Do you think he'll like it?

00:06:07.139 --> 00:06:10.139
I think he'll love it.

00:06:10.139 --> 00:06:15.139
But what is it exactly about a telescope that merits 76 trombones and a big parade?

00:06:15.139 --> 00:06:19.139
Well, tonight's the night.

00:06:19.139 --> 00:06:24.139
In the words of the general, it's time to drop the album.

00:06:24.139 --> 00:06:25.139
What?

00:06:25.139 --> 00:06:28.139
You mean to tell me that you guys haven't volleyed the word yet?

00:06:28.139 --> 00:06:30.139
Among other significant relationships,

00:06:30.139 --> 00:06:33.139
other significant relationship milestones.

00:06:33.139 --> 00:06:34.139
I don't know.

00:06:34.139 --> 00:06:36.139
Things used to be easier with Clark.

00:06:36.139 --> 00:06:41.139
Back in the days when you'd wake up and the first thing you'd do is check for a text or an email

00:06:41.139 --> 00:06:43.139
and be there waiting for you?

00:06:43.139 --> 00:06:46.139
Anyway, things have been different.

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:49.139
Ever since we decided we could keep secrets from each other.

00:06:49.139 --> 00:06:52.139
But that's all changing tonight.

00:06:52.139 --> 00:06:55.139
Wait a minute. Secrets?

00:06:55.139 --> 00:06:57.139
Uh, changing how?

00:06:57.139 --> 00:07:00.379
No more secrets.

00:07:00.379 --> 00:07:01.379
It's time.

00:07:01.379 --> 00:07:03.379
to take our baggage out of the closet.

00:07:03.379 --> 00:07:08.379
I mean, if we all each other, then nothing should come between us, right?

00:07:08.379 --> 00:07:31.379
You ever check your voicemail?

00:07:31.379 --> 00:07:33.379
Looks like somebody missed breakfast in bed with Oliver this morning.

00:07:33.379 --> 00:07:35.379
I'm not here to talk about my love life.

00:07:35.379 --> 00:07:36.379
That makes two of us.

00:07:36.379 --> 00:07:37.379
I'm here to talk about yours.

00:07:37.379 --> 00:07:40.379
Whoa, can we just stick to a topic like aliens assimilating to Earth?

00:07:40.379 --> 00:07:43.379
This isn't about assimilating, Clark. Zad has powers now.

00:07:43.379 --> 00:07:45.379
And you told him all of your secrets.

00:07:45.379 --> 00:07:47.379
This is not a good time to bring Lois in, too.

00:07:47.379 --> 00:07:48.379
Lois?

00:07:48.379 --> 00:07:49.379
Yeah.

00:07:49.379 --> 00:07:51.379
She told me about your big date tonight where you both are going to come clean with you?

00:07:51.379 --> 00:07:53.379
are going to come clean with everything?

00:07:53.379 --> 00:07:55.379
I'm not going to tell Lois anything.

00:07:55.379 --> 00:07:58.379
I'm making Lois dinner tonight, so she shares her secret.

00:07:58.379 --> 00:08:00.379
She's been keeping something from me.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:02.379
I didn't want to use my abilities to spy on her.

00:08:02.379 --> 00:08:03.379
It's been driving me crazy.

00:08:03.379 --> 00:08:05.379
So you're going to seduce it out of her?

00:08:05.379 --> 00:08:08.379
Clark, you're the reason all of this is happening to begin with.

00:08:08.379 --> 00:08:09.379
I have not called her as a blur in months.

00:08:09.379 --> 00:08:11.379
That doesn't matter, Clark.

00:08:11.379 --> 00:08:13.379
The second that you're back in black alter ego

00:08:13.379 --> 00:08:15.379
asked Lois to lie about the blur was the day that you

00:08:15.379 --> 00:08:17.379
asked her to lie to the person that she loves,

00:08:17.379 --> 00:08:18.379
which is you.

00:08:18.379 --> 00:08:24.120
And she did.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:25.120
A relationship with secrets.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.120
can never work.

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.120
Look at you and Oliver.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:28.120
Everything's out in the open.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:30.120
That is because we both understand that our relationship

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:33.120
comes second to a higher calling.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:34.120
Clark, you and Lois...

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:36.120
Don't have to be any different.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:37.120
Now, if Lois was gonna trust me tonight,

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.120
maybe it's time I trusted her.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:09:05.059
Did you argue my message?

00:09:05.059 --> 00:09:06.059
Yep.

00:09:06.059 --> 00:09:10.970
So we're still on for tonight?

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:18.059
Definitely.

00:09:18.059 --> 00:09:19.059
What's in the box?

00:09:19.059 --> 00:09:22.200
Surprise.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:26.820
It's gonna be a long day.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:30.700
Yep.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:47.899
How about a sneak preview?

00:09:47.899 --> 00:09:49.899
Sometimes I swear you have more than two hands.

00:09:49.899 --> 00:09:56.490
Either that kiss altered my sense of time and space,

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:58.490
or this place is busier than usual.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:09:59.490
It's a big news day.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.490
I think it has something to do with our new editor.

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:02.490
Another editor?

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:04.490
They should just install a rotating door up there.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:07.490
Obviously, our illustrious owners just spun some big wheel of fortune

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:10.490
in the sky to see we'd be steering the ship this week.

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:19.299
Well, I guess I pulled the lucky number this week.

00:10:19.299 --> 00:10:21.299
Franklin Starr.

00:10:21.299 --> 00:10:26.299
And this live way must be the lovely and charming Miss Lane, I presume.

00:10:26.299 --> 00:10:28.299
Miss Lane is an acquired taste.

00:10:28.299 --> 00:10:33.500
It's just that ever since Tess went away,

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:35.500
we've gone through a lot of editors.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.500
Well, not for long.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:41.500
The board just launched a global search for the next editor-in-chief.

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:44.500
I intend to make their decision very easy.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:49.500
And you decided to start your campaign by downsizing the desk inventory.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:52.779
Ms. Lane.

00:10:52.779 --> 00:10:57.779
I have been reading through the personnel files

00:10:57.779 --> 00:10:58.779
to identify any red flyer.

00:10:58.779 --> 00:11:00.779
to find any red flags.

00:11:00.779 --> 00:11:05.779
And I understand you two are entangled in an inner office relationship?

00:11:05.779 --> 00:11:07.779
No, sir.

00:11:07.779 --> 00:11:13.940
For whatever reason.

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:16.940
It seems you're both spending so much time out of the office

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:18.940
trying to reel in the big fish.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.940
You're not delivering the daily catch.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:23.940
To be fair, sir, we've both turned in some pretty big stories.

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:25.940
Here's a bigger one.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:28.940
Our fair city's disgraced D.A. Ray Sacks

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:31.940
just had his life sentence reversed.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:33.940
He gets out of prison today.

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:39.919
Only one of these stays on the desk at the end of the day.

00:11:39.919 --> 00:11:44.960
May the best reporter win.

00:11:44.960 --> 00:12:33.139
Oliver gave you keys to his office.

00:12:33.139 --> 00:12:36.139
He must trust you with just about all of his secrets.

00:12:36.139 --> 00:12:38.139
Tess.

00:12:38.139 --> 00:12:40.139
I thought she were supposed to be underground.

00:12:40.139 --> 00:12:43.139
You know, if you're having a hard time finding your way there, I'm sure I could help.

00:12:43.139 --> 00:12:46.649
So we're over the temporary truce.

00:12:46.649 --> 00:12:49.649
And straight back to fire it, well...

00:12:49.649 --> 00:12:51.649
Okay.

00:12:51.649 --> 00:12:53.649
Just remember, Chloe, that out there I might be MIA,

00:12:53.649 --> 00:12:54.649
but in here,

00:12:54.649 --> 00:12:56.649
here, I'm still CEO.

00:12:56.649 --> 00:13:06.009
Where is Oliver?

00:13:06.009 --> 00:13:13.120
Out of town?

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:17.120
I was curious how you two got into each other's orbit.

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:19.120
Mutual friends.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:22.120
Which I understand you could use some help finding,

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:25.120
considering the fact that you have to go to outer space to look for them.

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:28.460
The Candorians?

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:30.460
You'll see, Chloe.

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:32.460
They're better as allies than enemies.

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:34.460
Clark gets that.

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:36.460
Why don't you and Oliver?

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:38.460
Clark optimistically thinks that Zad will be happy.

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:41.460
thinks that Zod will be happy wearing an apron and slinging coffees.

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:43.460
We don't.

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:48.480
Especially now that he has powers.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:54.370
We? As in you and Green Arrow?

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:58.370
Chloe, I get what you see in your heroes.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:00.370
But what do they see in you?

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:04.679
I could ask Zod the same question about you,

00:14:04.679 --> 00:14:06.679
but I guess I don't have to anymore.

00:14:06.679 --> 00:14:07.679
I've been watching you too.

00:14:07.679 --> 00:14:10.679
And it seems like Zod hasn't been home for dinner for quite a while.

00:14:10.679 --> 00:14:15.240
Be careful, Miss Mercer.

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:30.529
At this rate, you're going to run out of people to betray.

00:14:30.529 --> 00:14:31.529
I don't know what's worse, Clark,

00:14:31.529 --> 00:14:33.529
that they freed the DA that threw me off the roof

00:14:33.529 --> 00:14:36.529
or that our editor threw us in the ring to rest with the same desk.

00:14:36.529 --> 00:14:37.529
Don't worry.

00:14:37.529 --> 00:14:39.529
If we land a big enough story, we can save both our jobs.

00:14:39.529 --> 00:14:41.529
Now, in order for him to reverse his sentence,

00:14:41.529 --> 00:14:44.529
Sacks must still have powerful friends down in City Hall.

00:14:44.529 --> 00:14:46.529
And according to the underground blogs,

00:14:46.529 --> 00:14:48.529
he's having a welcome home party tonight at Maxwell's.

00:14:48.529 --> 00:14:50.529
Crime Kingpins like to keep out the outsiders.

00:14:50.529 --> 00:14:53.529
It'd be easier to crash the White House than it would be to sneak into that party.

00:14:53.529 --> 00:14:58.320
Look, we only have till the end of the day to get this done.

00:14:58.320 --> 00:14:59.320
I think we'd cover more ground if we split the outside.

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:00.320
work.

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:05.259
That's good idea.

00:15:05.259 --> 00:15:06.259
Can't wait for tonight.

00:15:06.259 --> 00:15:16.259
Hey, it's me. Lois.

00:15:16.259 --> 00:15:17.259
Guess you're out.

00:15:17.259 --> 00:15:20.259
It's strange to think that I can leave a message for the blur.

00:15:20.259 --> 00:15:21.259
I mean, well, not strange, weird.

00:15:21.259 --> 00:15:22.259
It's just, you know what I mean.

00:15:22.259 --> 00:15:24.259
It's hard to picture the blur.

00:15:24.259 --> 00:15:25.259
Screening us calls.

00:15:25.259 --> 00:15:27.259
Not that you'd be screening my calls or anything, but I didn't.

00:15:27.259 --> 00:15:29.259
Me again, got cut off.

00:15:29.259 --> 00:15:32.259
You know, that's not a lot of time for someone to leave a message.

00:15:32.259 --> 00:15:34.259
That beep comes out to you pretty fast.

00:15:34.259 --> 00:15:35.259
Then again, you are the blur.

00:15:35.259 --> 00:15:38.259
Of course, I'm sure you like it fast, but I just...

00:15:38.259 --> 00:15:39.259
Here's the deal.

00:15:39.259 --> 00:15:40.259
I'm on a story about a story about you.

00:15:40.259 --> 00:15:41.259
our deadly XDA.

00:15:41.259 --> 00:15:43.259
Now, normally I'd be working with my partner in reporting,

00:15:43.259 --> 00:15:45.259
but I want to keep him safe, secure,

00:15:45.259 --> 00:15:49.259
and as far away from Sacks and as murderous mob as I can.

00:15:49.259 --> 00:15:51.259
Clark's not bulletproof, but you are.

00:15:51.259 --> 00:15:58.539
Be my wingman.

00:15:58.539 --> 00:16:01.539
Lois will find a way to see Sacks before the party tonight.

00:16:01.539 --> 00:16:02.539
Chloe, I have to find him first.

00:16:02.539 --> 00:16:03.539
Look, I get it, Clark.

00:16:03.539 --> 00:16:05.539
I'm spending a small fortune of Oliver's money

00:16:05.539 --> 00:16:07.539
to update the security system here at Watchtower.

00:16:07.539 --> 00:16:09.539
Plus, I have a satellite trained on your fortress

00:16:09.539 --> 00:16:11.539
at all times now that Zod knows your zip code.

00:16:11.539 --> 00:16:14.539
I understand the instinct to protect the ones that you love.

00:16:14.539 --> 00:16:15.539
You know, half of being in a relationship.

00:16:15.539 --> 00:16:17.539
You're half of being in a relationship with Lois

00:16:17.539 --> 00:16:19.539
is protecting her from herself.

00:16:19.539 --> 00:16:22.539
Actually, she's not the only one Sacks is gunning for right now.

00:16:22.539 --> 00:16:25.539
According to the internet, he's offering a million dollar reward

00:16:25.539 --> 00:16:28.539
for anyone who can supply him with an image of the blur.

00:16:28.539 --> 00:16:31.539
Again, what's with this guy in his obsession with the blur?

00:16:31.539 --> 00:16:35.539
Maybe it has something to do with the fact you publicly disgraced him and threw him in prison.

00:16:35.539 --> 00:16:39.539
Since he's been out, I have hard time tracking him down.

00:16:39.539 --> 00:16:42.539
Well, Sacks is all about the VIP treatment.

00:16:42.539 --> 00:16:44.539
Maybe he's got a favorite bar or restaurant.

00:16:44.539 --> 00:16:48.190
Someplace that's a place that he's been out.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:51.190
he would want to go to after being locked down for eight months.

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:53.190
Huh.

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:56.190
Our parole prosecutor does have a favorite haunt.

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:59.190
But it isn't exactly five star.

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:12.500
Mr. Sacks, Lois Lane from the Daily Planet.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:15.500
You may remember me from the roof of the Daily Planet.

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:18.500
Oh, yes. Yes, I remember you.

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:22.500
You have a nasty habit of always landing on your feet, don't you, Lane?

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:24.500
And now I need to land a story.

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:26.500
So who let you out of your cage?

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:28.500
Since I'm the one that you stand.

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:30.500
skydiving without a parachute,

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:32.500
I figure I'm at least owed a quote.

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:34.500
You have too much faith in the blur lane

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:38.500
to think you can meet with me like this alone.

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:44.019
My editor knows where I am.

00:17:44.019 --> 00:17:48.019
Hurt me, and you'll be back behind bars before this pizza cools off.

00:17:48.019 --> 00:17:50.019
Oh, I won't hurt you, no.

00:17:50.019 --> 00:17:52.019
He will.

00:17:52.019 --> 00:17:55.019
And this time, they won't find me guilty because

00:17:55.019 --> 00:17:57.019
they'll never find your body.

00:17:57.019 --> 00:18:25.450
It's him, come on.

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:26.450
Thank you.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:27.450
For saving my bacon, I'd be too.

00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:29.450
I'd be two strips of pain on the pavement

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:31.450
if you hadn't gotten my call.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:36.329
You have no idea what it means

